# WazHack/ZX B10 open-door jambs + lair exit grate — DRAFT for user review (2026-10-03).
# Format = tools/gfx_convert.py --mode tile (same as door.tiles).
# Open door (plan B10): the opening rows 9s+2..9s+7 stamp door_jamb_l / door_jamb_r instead
# of AIR. Both are NON-solid, ink $06 on black like the arch. One glyph per side, repeated
# down all 6 opening rows (2 new tile ids).
#   door_jamb_l  = proposal A: arch outer double stroke (cols 0,2) continued + the open
#                  leaf seen edge-on (cols 4-5, hinge side = left; the lock is on the right
#                  plank) with a hinge strap on band row 3 (the planks' iron band row).
#   door_jamb_lp = proposal B (staff): plain double stroke, no leaf. Same id, pick one.
#   door_jamb_r  = arch outer double stroke (cols 5,7) continued.
# Grate (T_GRATE, id 26): per game.md §1.1/§3.3 and concept-screen §3.3 the lair grate lies
# OVER the down-exit hole {c,2} in floor row 17 (3x1, one glyph repeated, attr $07). Side
# view: top bar (walkable), crossbar, 2-px iron bars with the black shaft between them.
